\section{Model and Logistic metric (D = 1)}{

All native models use the logistic metric with \eqn{D = 1} (no \code{1.7}/\code{1.702}
multiplier). For additive \code{RSM}/\code{PCM} with Person \eqn{n}, rater \eqn{j},
and criterion \eqn{i}:
\deqn{\ln\frac{P(X_{nij} = k)}{P(X_{nij} = k-1)} =
  \theta_n - \delta_j - \beta_i - \tau_k}
(\code{RSM} shares \eqn{\tau_k}; \code{PCM} estimates \eqn{\tau_{i,k}} per \code{step_facet}
level; binary \code{K = 1} reduces to \eqn{\eta - \tau_1}). Confirmatory
\code{facet_interactions} add \eqn{+\gamma_{ji}} with \eqn{\sum_j\gamma_{ji} = 0}
and \eqn{\sum_i\gamma_{ji} = 0}. One-family \code{GPCM} scales the complete
adjacent-category predictor:
\deqn{\ln\frac{P(X_{nij} = k)}{P(X_{nij} = k-1)} =
  \alpha_g(\eta - \tau_{h,k}),\quad \alpha_g > 0,\quad \prod_{g=1}^G \alpha_g^{1/G} = 1.}
Because \eqn{\alpha_g} multiplies \eqn{\theta_n}, all facet locations, and
\eqn{\tau_{h,k}}, it differs from loading-only formulations where slopes
multiply \eqn{\theta_n} alone.

Uncorrected JML jointly maximizes fixed Person and structural parameters
without finite bounds or the dichotomous \eqn{(L-1)/L} heuristic, subject to
Neyman-Scott incidental-parameter bias at fixed ratings per Person
(Haberman, 2004). Exploratory JML location SEs use observation-table
information \eqn{\mathrm{SE}_g \approx [\sum_{r \in g} w_r a_r^2
\mathrm{Var}(X_r \mid \widehat\eta_r)]^{-1/2}} (\code{Fixed = TRUE} rows keep
\code{NA} SEs). Extreme free JML Persons return \code{-Inf}/\code{Inf} in \code{Estimate} (with
computational trace in \code{OptimizerEstimate}); MML integrates Persons over the
declared normal prior and reports post-hoc EAPs and posterior SDs.
}

\section{Two slope families}{

Setting \code{model = "GPCM"}, \code{method = "MML"}, \code{slope_facet = c(F1, F2)},
\code{gpcm_mml_identification = "fixed_standard_normal"}, and explicit
\code{step_facet} and \code{noncenter_facet} fits the multiplicative Uto and Ueno
(2020) predictor \eqn{\alpha_{1,g}\alpha_{2,m}(\eta - \tau_{h,k})} on one
fixed \eqn{N(0,1)} ability dimension using unweighted zero-based integer
scores (\code{0:rating_max}), with either fixed-grid \code{"em"} or adaptive
\code{"direct"} MML. \code{slope_reference} fixes one slope family's geometric mean to
\code{1} while the second family is free. Experimental component-slope, step, and
location intervals (\code{\link[=confint.mfrm_fit]{confint.mfrm_fit()}}, \code{\link[=mfrm_facet_intervals]{mfrm_facet_intervals()}}),
fixed-calibration posterior residuals (\code{\link[=mfrm_response_diagnostics]{mfrm_response_diagnostics()}}), and
conditional scoring (\code{\link[=predict_mfrm_units]{predict_mfrm_units()}}) retain separate numerical
checks; Wright maps, ordinary fit diagnostics, and IC ranking remain
unavailable (see \link{mfrmr_gpcm_scope}).
}

\section{Corrected JML}{

Positive integer \code{jml_correction_order = k} solves the adjusted profile-score
equation \eqn{U_k = (I - K_\beta)^k U_0 = 0} (Dhaene & Weidner, 2023,
Section 8.1) for additive shared-owner GPCM JML with preserved integer
categories (\verb{<= 5,000} joint owner-total states per assignment pattern; no
anchors, weights, interactions, or shrinkage). Empirical Person-contribution
Jacobians yield \code{RootSE} and \code{LogRootSE} under \code{"fixed_rosters"} or
\code{"random_rosters"}; these describe local root variation rather than
coverage-qualified structural confidence intervals.
}

\section{Jeffreys-penalized JML}{

Setting \verb{method = "JML", jml_penalty = "jeffreys"} on identified unit-weight
additive RSM/PCM with preserved \code{rating_min:rating_max} minimizes
\eqn{-\ell(\beta) - \tfrac12\log|I(\beta)|} in affine free canonical
coordinates (Firth, 1993; Kosmidis & Firth, 2021), returning
\code{mfrm_jeffreys_fit} (\code{\link[=summary.mfrm_jeffreys_fit]{summary.mfrm_jeffreys_fit()}}) with point estimates and
numerical checks (\code{checks$polish}), connecting to common-plan expected-score
intervals in \code{\link[=confint.mfrm_fair_average]{confint.mfrm_fair_average()}} without Wald parameter SEs or ICs.
}

\section{Conditional maximum likelihood}{

Setting \verb{method = "CML", category_policy = "preserve"} on unit-weight
additive or two-way-interaction RSM/PCM conditions on Person totals
\eqn{s_p = \sum_j y_{pj}}:
\deqn{\ell_c(\beta) = \sum_{p,j} x_{pj,y_{pj}}^\top\beta -
  \sum_p \log [t^{s_p}] \prod_j \sum_{k=0}^K \exp(x_{pjk}^\top\beta)t^k,}
evaluated via log-scale generalized ESF recursions with dynamic-programming
LP recession checks (\code{lpSolve}). Full-scope CML returns \code{mfrm_cml_fit} with
unregularized inverse conditional-information \code{covariance} (\code{NA} matrix with
\code{checks$information_status = "unavailable"} if singular) and connects to
\code{\link[=mfrm_facet_intervals]{mfrm_facet_intervals()}} without Person or population parameters (Mair &
Hatzinger, 2007).
}

\section{Comparison-only estimation}{

Setting \code{fit_scope = "comparisons"} with a prospective \code{comparison_review}
returns \code{mfrm_comparison_fit} for identifiable facet-by-origin contrasts in
rank-deficient designs (\code{nrow(A)*ncol(A) <= 2e6}, \code{ncol(A)^2 <= 2e6}). JML
and MML project onto the column-scaled SVD range and report
\code{descriptive_only} contrast points (\code{FormalInferenceEligible = FALSE}). CML
optimizes in the conditional support-difference subspace \eqn{\beta =
T\gamma + v} (\eqn{Cv = 0}) with basis-invariant covariance
\eqn{CT(T^\top I_N T)^{-1}T^\top C^\top} (\code{EstimateStatus = "conditional_wald"} or \code{"conditional_point"}), distinguishing estimability
(Lenth, 2015) from exponential-family recession cones (Geyer, 2009,
\doi{10.1214/08-EJS349}).
}

\section{Latent-regression workflow}{

With \code{method = "MML"}, \code{population_formula}, and one-row-per-Person
\code{person_data}, Person quadrature nodes follow \eqn{\theta_{nq} =
x_n^\top\beta + \sigma z_q}. \code{summary(fit)$population_coefficients} and
\verb{$population_overview} report point estimates without automatic SEs; request
experimental joint-information intervals via \code{\link[=mfrm_population_intervals]{mfrm_population_intervals()}}
(RSM/PCM). In anchored RSM/PCM cohorts, \code{noncenter_facet = "Rater"} with a
direct Rater anchor and \code{population_formula = ~ 1} (optionally fixed
\code{population_sd}) estimates the receiving-cohort mean without forcing new
raters to sum to zero.
}

\section{Pre-fit estimability and Information-criterion contract}{

Before optimization, sparse adjacent-logit rank checks stop exact rank
deficiency with \code{mfrmr_estimability_error} and warn (\code{mfrmr_estimability_warning})
when MML cross-panel contrasts rely solely on a shared population
(\code{fit$data_review$estimability}, including \code{normal_population_identification}
and \code{nonlinear_local_estimability}).

For eligible unit-weight \code{MML} fits with \code{D = -2 * LogLik}, free dimension
\code{k = Npar}, and unique prepared Persons \code{N_person} (\code{ICSampleSize}), the
canonical panel is \code{AIC = D + 2*k}, \code{BIC = D + log(N_person)*k}, and
\code{SABIC = D + log((N_person + 2)/24)*k} (\code{SABICSelectable = FALSE} when
\code{N_person <= 22}). Ineligible fits set canonical \code{AIC}/\code{BIC}/\code{SABIC} to \code{NA}
(\code{LegacyAIC}/\code{LegacyBIC} retained separately). \code{ICIntegrationTier} classifies
\code{quad_points} (\verb{< 15} \code{"coarse_screening"}, \code{15:30} \code{"intermediate_review"},
\code{31:60} \code{"standard_start"}, \verb{>= 61} \code{"dense_sensitivity"}), with
\code{ICSelectable = FALSE} below \code{31} points in \code{\link[=compare_mfrm]{compare_mfrm()}}.
}

\section{Detailed return-object provenance}{

Depending on estimator and scope, \code{fit_mfrm()} returns \code{mfrm_jeffreys_fit},
\code{mfrm_cml_fit}, \code{mfrm_comparison_fit}, or a named \code{mfrm_fit} list with:
\code{summary} (fit metrics, IC contract, convergence, optimizer controls),
\code{facets$person} (\code{Estimate}, MML \code{SD}, \code{Extreme}, \code{SourceFitReadiness},
\code{EstimateUse}), \code{facets$others}, \code{steps}, \code{slopes} (\code{OptimizerEstimate},
\code{PrimaryEstimate}, \code{ParameterStatus}, \code{SEEligible}, \code{CIEligible},
\code{ReasonCodes}, plus \code{point_limit} and \code{config$boundary_audit} records),
\code{readiness}, \code{interactions}, \code{population} (\code{person_table},
\code{person_table_replay}, \code{xlevels}, \code{contrasts}, \code{estimation_converged},
\code{inference_ready}), \code{data_review}, \code{config}, \code{prep}, and \code{opt}
(\code{optimizer_diagnostics}, \code{optimizer_polish}, \code{start_review},
\code{mml_initialization}).
}

